Assistant: Could you describe the core messaging and buddy-list capabilities the application must support, including any specific rules for presence updates, nickname management, blocking contacts, and message notifications?
User: The application needs to let a user send and receive plain text instant messages with people on their buddy list, and it should show which buddies are currently online and, when available, what program or channel they’re watching. Users should be able to add and remove buddies, see their presence status update in near real time, and change their own nickname so it’s reflected to others. If a contact is blocked, that person should no longer be able to message the user or appear as available in the normal buddy view, and incoming messages should trigger a clear visible on-screen notification so the user knows something has arrived even if they’re not actively in the chat.

